1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Catharina (Carin) Wulff, née Gyzander''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1806-1857)
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of first land surveyor (förste lantmätare) Joh. Laur. Gyzander and his wife Lovisa Catharina, née Gerss. Cartharina married Claes Fredrik Wulff and was the mother of, among others, Professor Fredrik Wulff. Notes by Fredri
2 CONC k Wulff, most notably on the inside of the front cover, where he has written a short biography of his mother. The album contains c. 60 entries. Eight loose sheets of paper, on the first a pencil drawing (1v), on the second the poe
2 CONC m “Söndagsmorgonen” by Laurentius Börgesson, vice vicar of Tölö (2r), on the third a transcription made “Till Sophie” by “Annie Elise” of the text of a play (19r-19v), on the fourth a letter from “Sophie” (Söderborg?) (22r), on th
2 CONC e fifth a poem from C. A. (35r), on the sixth a painting by J. W. Gerss, on the seventh a poem from Isabella Geber (44r), on the eighth an autograph by Robert Bendsen ? (47r). (N.B: The pencil drawing, the poem "Söndagsmorgonen", 
2 CONC the transcription "Till Sophie" and the letter from Sophie have been photographed separately and can be seen after the text of the album). Many verses on friendship, mostly in Swedish. Numerous entries by members of the Gyzander a
2 CONC nd Gerss families. Locks of hair, paintings and embroidery. No pagination.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.alvin-portal.org/alvin/view.jsf?pid=alvin-record%3A192075&dswid=8910
