1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Catharina Maria Martinel (1773-1813) Housewife (b. 1773, Jämtland, Sweden - d. November 26, 1813, Hede, Jämtland, Sweden)
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in 1773, in Jämtland, Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Johan Christopher Örbom Ruuth (1767-1822) Vicar of Hede, Sweden. Johan was the son of Erik Johan Örbom (1723/24-1815), Major of the Jämtland regiment; and Helena Ruuth (1729-1822), aka Helena von der Hude. Johan took h
2 CONC is mother's maiden name and made it his family name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children: Catharina Helena Ruut (1797-?) who was born in Linsell, married Michael Huss (1782-1836), a vicar and they lived in Mo; Johanna Gustafva Ruuth (1800-1860) who married Israel Israelsson Näslund III 
2 CONC (1796-1858); Eric Gustav Ruuth (1803-1864) who was a student in 1822 and later joined the King's Guard; Jacob Efraim Ruuth (1808-?) who was born in Hult and went to school in Härnösand and traveled to Finland with an acting group,
2 CONC  that later came to St. Petersburg where he first became a teacher and then obtained a counsellor position; Kristina Margarita Ruuth (1810-?) born in Hede and married Carl Gustav Högström, a bookbinder in 1833, they lived in Öster
2 CONC sund; Carl Johan Ruuth (1812-1832) who was born in Hede and commited suicide on December 28, 1832 in the Stallmästargården (the stable master's house) in Stockholm; and Maria Elizabeth Ruuth (1813-1815).
2 CONT
2 CONT Death:
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on November 26, 1813, Hede, Jämtland, Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship:
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharina Maria Martinel (1773-1813) was the fourth great-grandfather of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ). 
