1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Johanna Gustafva Ruuth (1800-1860) Housewife (b. January 11, 1800, Linsell socken, Krokom kommun, Jämtland län, Sweden - d. February 15, 1860, Ytterlännäs, Västernorrlands, Sweden) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: She was the daughter of Catharina Martinel (1773-1813) and Johan Christopher Ruuth (1767-1822). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: She married Israel Israelsson Näslund III (1796-1858) at Östbacken, Hede, Västernorrlands, Sweden on March 23, 1821. Israel was the 18th Assistant Vicar at Torsåker, Sweden and the Vicar in Ytterlännäs, Hede and Torsåker
2 CONC , Sweden. He died of smallpox during an epidemic in 1858. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Together they had the following children: Johan Israel Näslund (1822-1906) who married Emma Maria Falk (1817-1860); Carl Gustaf Näslund (1825-1899) who became the Vicar of Arnäs, Sweden from 1872 to 1889, and married Kri
2 CONC stina Carolina Sjöström (1839-?); Elsa Maria Elisabeth Näslund (1829-?) a twin of Olof, who married Anton Julius Winblad I (1828-1901) a schoolteacher and church organist at Ytterlännäs, Sweden; Olof Emanuel Näslund (1829-1906) a 
2 CONC twin of Elsa who married Annette Brandell (1820-?); and Johanna Näslund (1838-?).
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship: Johanna Gustafva Ruuth (1800-1860) was the third, great-grandmother of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Researched and written by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) for Findagrave starting on January 4, 2004. 
